Create:

### Days 1–30
Technical foundation + UX + indexing + quality

### Days 31–60
Content + topical authority + internal linking

### Days 61–90
SERP expansion + tools + optimization + authority

---

# 12–24 MONTH ORGANIC GROWTH ROADMAP

Model the evolution:

**Foundation**

→

**Search visibility**

→

**Topical authority**

→

**Organic growth**

→

**Market authority**

→

**Scale**

Identify what must change at each stage.

---

# DEFINITION OF DONE

The website is NOT considered production-ready merely because it compiles.

It must satisfy:

[ ] Production build succeeds

[ ] Critical routes work

[ ] Direct URLs work

[ ] Refreshing routes works

[ ] Important functionality works

[ ] Forms work

[ ] Error states work

[ ] Mobile UX works

[ ] No critical broken links

[ ] Sitemap works

[ ] Robots.txt works

[ ] Canonicals are correct

[ ] Metadata is unique and useful

[ ] Structured data is accurate

[ ] Important pages are indexable

[ ] Low-value pages are controlled

[ ] No serious cannibalization

[ ] Internal linking is logical

[ ] Content is genuinely useful

[ ] Content reads naturally

[ ] No keyword stuffing

[ ] No mass-produced low-value content

[ ] Search intent is satisfied

[ ] Competitor gaps have been identified

[ ] Performance is acceptable

[ ] Accessibility is acceptable

[ ] Security issues are addressed

[ ] Analytics/measurement is ready

[ ] Conversion paths are clear

[ ] Monetization does not damage UX

[ ] Architecture can scale

[ ] Content architecture can scale

[ ] SEO architecture can scale

[ ] The site has a credible path toward substantial organic growth

[ ] Final stress test passes

---

# FINAL PRINCIPLE

Do not optimize this website merely to "look SEO optimized."

Build something that deserves to win.

The standard is:

**Better product + better UX + better content + better technical foundation + better search-intent coverage + better information architecture + continuous measurement and improvement.**

Do not chase 1M traffic by creating 10,000 mediocre pages.

Build the smallest number of high-value assets capable of capturing the largest amount of relevant search demand.

If an existing page is weak, improve it.

If two pages compete, consolidate them.

If a page has no legitimate search purpose, remove or noindex it.

If a competitor has a better experience, understand why.

If an opportunity requires a tool rather than an article, build the tool.

If the current architecture prevents scalable SEO, fix the architecture.

Be critical.

Be evidence-driven.

Do not tell me what I want to hear.

Tell me what is actually preventing this website from becoming a serious organic-growth competitor—and then fix as much of it as the codebase allows.